    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on July 31, 2026, the engine is roaring behind **Corbin Carroll** (84.02), who projects as the clear anchor of the lineup against Tanner Bibee. The combination of an elite batting order slot (#1) and a favorable matchup pushes **Corbin Carroll** into the high-upside tier. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (75.74) is an unexpected value play today; despite a lower base projection, the aggressive 14% boost from park factors and platoon advantage against Michael Wacha makes him our most efficient sleeper. We are also looking for a significant boost in the speed category from **Brice Turang** (73.39), who faces Ryan Johnson. While Johnson\u2019s 4.79 xERA is soft, **Brice Turang**\u2019s leadoff positioning and 19% SP skill multiplier outweigh the minor negative impact of the opponent's catcher defensive metrics.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins involves **Austin Riley** (49.17), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Austin Riley** carries a strong historical profile, his projected #8 spot in the lineup and the relative difficulty of facing Foster Griffin created a scoring ceiling that couldn't crack the top 12. Consequently, we are leaning into the platoon-advantaged **Zach McKinstry** (63.74) for his park-boosted upside against Jeffrey Springs. Managers should remain vigilant regarding **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Cole Young**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Mickey Moniak**, **James Wood**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Corbin Carroll**; as all carry \"Lineup Pending\" status, a late-hour scratch could necessitate a pivot to **Travis Bazzana** or **Dalton Rushing**. \n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly for **Jose Caballero** (56.68) and **Zach McKinstry**. Both players face \"Elite Hold\" pitchers, meaning the stolen base potential\u2014the lifeblood of our team strategy\u2014is dampened by the opposing battery's ability to control the run game. We are officially marking **Vinnie Pasquantino** as unavailable due to his IL designation, removing any temptation to force him into the lineup. Monitor the official lineups closely; if **Cole Young** or **Brice Turang** shift out of the leadoff spot, we may see their scores regress as their categorical efficiency drops.",
